# Catalog documentation mirror

The `services/catalog/` code and `docs/catalog-architecture.md` must not drift apart.

## When this applies

You just read, edited, or created a file under `services/catalog/`.

## What to do

After finishing a significant change in `services/catalog/` — new service, changed
responsibility boundaries, renamed module, changed data flow or API contract —
mirror the change in `docs/catalog-architecture.md` before finishing the task:

1. Open `docs/catalog-architecture.md` and locate the section describing the
   component you changed.
2. Update the section to reflect the new reality (component list, interactions,
   invariants). Keep the wording consistent with the rest of the document.
3. If the change introduces a new component, add it to the architecture diagram
   source and regenerate if the repo has a script for it.

Cosmetic changes (formatting, comments, import order) do not require a doc update.
When unsure whether a change is significant, update the doc anyway — a redundant
paragraph costs less than a stale architecture document.
